{"audit_run_id":"audit:6059446a561e42b58a3589dd1180983e","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":87,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"The analysis uses `green_roof_survey.csv`. One row is one surveyed green roof: each of"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"the 44 extensive green roofs in the city was visited once in late summer and measured"},{"end_column":66,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"for all five outcomes on that visit. There are no missing values."},{"end_column":27,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"| Column | What it holds |"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"| --- | --- |"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"| `roof_id` | Short roof identifier, `GR01` to `GR44`, in survey visit order |"},{"end_column":106,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"| `substrate_depth` | Depth class: `shallow` (about 60 mm, 22 roofs) or `deep` (about 120 mm, 22 roofs) |"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"| `plant_richness_count` | Vascular plant species richness, count of species |"},{"end_column":61,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"| `veg_cover_pct` | Vegetation cover, percent of roof area |"},{"end_column":89,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"| `substrate_moisture_pct` | Substrate volumetric moisture in the survey week, percent |"},{"end_column":114,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"| `temp_reduction_c` | Midday surface temperature reduction against the adjacent bare membrane, degrees Celsius |"},{"end_column":117,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"| `invert_abundance_count` | Flying invertebrate catch from a standard 30 minute sticky trap, count of individuals |"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"The survey declared five outcome variables in advance, in the order listed above. Each"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"one was declared as its own ecological question about substrate depth, so each is"},{"end_column":58,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"compared between the two depth classes on its own merits."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"For every outcome the two groups are compared with a two-sample Student's t-test for"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"independent groups (`scipy.stats.ttest_ind`), the standard test for continuous"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"measurements from two separate sets of subjects. The 22 shallow roofs and the 22 deep"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"roofs are independent roofs, so nothing is paired. Significance is decided at the"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"conventional 0.05 threshold. All five comparisons are produced by `analysis.py`."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"Group means, test statistic, p-value and verdict, in the declared outcome order."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"| Outcome | Mean, shallow (n=22) | Mean, deep (n=22) | t | p | Verdict at 0.05 |"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| `plant_richness_count` | 7.95 | 12.86 | -8.152 | 3.44e-10 | Significant |"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"| `veg_cover_pct` | 63.33 | 80.23 | -7.780 | 1.14e-09 | Significant |"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"| `substrate_moisture_pct` | 10.87 | 17.42 | -10.377 | 3.68e-13 | Significant |"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"| `temp_reduction_c` | 6.26 | 6.84 | -1.116 | 0.271 | Not significant |"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"| `invert_abundance_count` | 33.18 | 37.27 | -0.851 | 0.400 | Not significant |"},{"end_column":13,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"Per outcome:"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"- **Plant species richness.** Deep roofs carried about 4.9 more vascular plant species"},{"end_column":56,"end_line":46,"start_column":3,"start_line":46,"text":"than shallow roofs (12.86 against 7.95). Significant."},{"end_column":84,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"- **Vegetation cover.** Deep roofs were about 16.9 percentage points greener (80.23"},{"end_column":47,"end_line":48,"start_column":3,"start_line":48,"text":"percent against 63.33 percent). Significant."},{"end_column":87,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"- **Substrate moisture.** Deep roofs held about 6.6 percentage points more moisture in"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":50,"start_column":3,"start_line":50,"text":"the survey week (17.42 percent against 10.87 percent). Significant."},{"end_column":86,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"- **Surface temperature reduction.** Deep roofs cooled the surface about 0.58 degrees"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":52,"start_column":3,"start_line":52,"text":"Celsius more than shallow roofs (6.84 against 6.26), and the roof-to-roof scatter is"},{"end_column":55,"end_line":53,"start_column":3,"start_line":53,"text":"wide enough that this difference is not significant."},{"end_column":86,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"- **Flying invertebrate abundance.** Deep roofs caught about 4.1 more individuals per"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":55,"start_column":3,"start_line":55,"text":"trap (37.27 against 33.18), again not significant against a very wide spread of"},{"end_column":11,"end_line":56,"start_column":3,"start_line":56,"text":"catches."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"Going from roughly 60 mm to roughly 120 mm of growing substrate is associated with a"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"clearly richer and greener roof that stays damper through late summer. Those three"},{"end_column":64,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"outcomes separate the two depth classes sharply in this survey."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":64,"start_column":1,"start_line":64,"text":"The two outcomes the team may care about for climate and biodiversity targets behave"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"differently. Both midday surface cooling and sticky-trap invertebrate catch were a"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"little higher on the deeper roofs, but in both cases the difference is small next to"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"how much individual roofs differ from each other, and neither reaches the 0.05"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"threshold here. On this evidence, specifying deeper substrate can be justified on"},{"end_column":84,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"vegetation and moisture grounds; it should not be sold on a promised gain in midday"},{"end_column":74,"end_line":70,"start_column":1,"start_line":70,"text":"cooling or in flying insect catch, which this survey did not demonstrate."},{"end_column":88,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"Two limits are worth stating plainly. This is a one-visit cross-sectional survey, so it"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"shows association between depth class and outcome, not proof that depth caused the"},{"end_column":84,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"difference; older, better-maintained, or better-sited roofs may also tend to be the"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"deeper ones. And a non-significant result here means this survey did not show a"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":76,"start_column":1,"start_line":76,"text":"difference, not that the difference is zero, especially for the two outcomes with the"},{"end_column":29,"end_line":77,"start_column":1,"start_line":77,"text":"widest roof-to-roof scatter."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:d3c3cd2b8be579358313","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:25a6625b983279563800db9fef428aaeb54def5d6ffab74a473d306d5eda31b2","end_line":77,"locator":"report.md:1-77","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
